# Village house wall, decorative and NON-solid (like railing_bg; D-041):
# cool whitewash in shade h with one window per tile (green G shutters with
# j panel lines, i frame, transom and sill, b glass with one s pane).
# Distinct from the solid facade_village (warm w body, w/i lip, m edges,
# timber storey): h body, no lip, no dark edges, never a timber storey.
# Edges only use i, so a wall next to a balcony cell (the balcony draws the
# same wall behind itself) still reads as one wall: exposed top = flat 1 px
# i eave shadow, exposed bottom = 2 px i base band, exposed right = 1 px i.
# Autotiled (D-020): anim `auto`, frame = neighbour mask
# (1 = same tile above, 2 = right, 4 = below, 8 = left; level edge = same).
sprite = tile_wall_village_bg
size   = 16x16
origin = 0,0
anim   = auto frames=16 ticks=1
---
